The "bad" tracking in the rpmkeys -K callback has no chance of working
correctly with multiple items where some might be disabled or missing.
Let rpmvsVerify() handle the calculation, and return the failed types
through its return code.

Make the rpmvsVerify() stuff more explicit as well: in enforcing modes,
we always require the full package range to be covered, and mixing
enforcing mode with RPMVSF_NEEDPAYLOAD needs to fail because it cannot
then cover the whole package. And then base the return code on the
coverage explicitly.

Add some commentary to this spaghetti while at it.

